{:edb/db-before-t 1785 :edb/db-after-t 1786 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535098 50 #inst "2026-10-08T16:46:33.192Z" 13194139535098 true] [17592186124380 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331053 13194139535098 true] [17592186124380 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331074 13194139535098 true] [17592186124381 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331060 13194139535098 true] [17592186124382 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331067 13194139535098 true] [17592186124382 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331081 13194139535098 true] [17592186331053 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331054 13194139535098 true] [17592186331053 1089 "q-130718" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331053 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535098 true] [17592186331053 1100 "Consider the plane curve ${x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}=6.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(3,1).$" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331053 1113 #uuid "185f66f3-9fba-5841-9ae6-a31944a1af0d" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331053 1145 "If we set $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-3{y}^{2},$ our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=6.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(3,1)$ can be found by computing $∇f(3,1).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(3,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =2x\\,i-6y\\,j \\\\ ∇f(3,1) & =2(3)\\,i-6(1)\\,j \\\\  & =6\\,i-6\\,j \\\\  & =⟨6,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(3,1)=⟨6,-6⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(3,1).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-3}{6} & =\\frac{y-1}{(-6)} \\\\ -6(x-3) & =6(y-1) \\\\ -(x-3) & =y-1 \\\\ -x+3 & =y-1 \\\\ x+y-4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331055 13194139535098 true] [17592186331054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331056 13194139535098 true] [17592186331054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331057 13194139535098 true] [17592186331054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331058 13194139535098 true] [17592186331054 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331059 13194139535098 true] [17592186331054 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535098 true] [17592186331054 1041 "selection" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331054 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331057 13194139535098 true] [17592186331054 1110 #uuid "6f798868-eff2-5e73-9471-09264f27a8c3" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331055 1034 "2x+y-7=0" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331055 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331055 1111 #uuid "76573843-ec78-585b-af82-bae778b83009" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331056 1034 "x+3y-6=0" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331056 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331056 1111 #uuid "5b2811c8-62aa-5a93-8981-18721a20ad59" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331057 1034 "x+y-4=0" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331057 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331057 1111 #uuid "83eed442-106f-5182-8a04-9b0e401c10cd" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331058 1034 "x-y-2=0" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331058 1111 #uuid "24db7740-142f-5ff4-ad09-89cffbccbd4c" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331059 1034 "x-3y=0" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331059 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331059 1111 #uuid "08936e67-0d0d-5760-a873-7da74707acef" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331060 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331061 13194139535098 true] [17592186331060 1089 "q-131115" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331060 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535098 true] [17592186331060 1100 "For the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz},$ find a vector that's perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,4,1).$" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331060 1113 #uuid "c83000c4-b29e-5b4d-9073-cd5d94e04a02" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331060 1145 "A normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,4,1)$ can be found by computing \n$∇f(1,4,1).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient and evaluate it at $(x,y,z)=(1,4,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz}+)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{xy}+\\sqrt{yz})\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{xy}}\\,i+(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{xy}}+\\frac{z}{2\\sqrt{yz}})j+\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{yz}}\\,k \\\\ ∇f(1,4,1) & =\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{1(4)}}\\,i+(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1(4)}}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4(1)}})j+\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{4(1)}}\\,k \\\\  & =i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+k$ is perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,4,1).$" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331061 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331062 13194139535098 true] [17592186331061 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331063 13194139535098 true] [17592186331061 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331064 13194139535098 true] [17592186331061 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331065 13194139535098 true] [17592186331061 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331066 13194139535098 true] [17592186331061 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535098 true] [17592186331061 1041 "selection" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331061 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331064 13194139535098 true] [17592186331061 1110 #uuid "84f8131f-da98-5ca7-8fec-b89d5f9e624f" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331062 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331062 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331062 1111 #uuid "b295344e-e699-5f9b-973c-133bb94797ac" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331063 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i-j+k" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331063 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331063 1111 #uuid "4dbaef38-07e5-5120-922c-f92b0bf12ef8" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331064 1034 "i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+k" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331064 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331064 1111 #uuid "8184a3fd-fd88-58f2-baeb-76fb0f7d30ca" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331065 1034 "i+\\frac{1}{4}\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331065 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331065 1111 #uuid "688b0570-33d1-547f-88ac-8355397694b7" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331066 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}\\,i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+k" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331066 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331066 1111 #uuid "5f0a8753-ae01-5ea7-a98c-333a2b9c7968" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331067 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331068 13194139535098 true] [17592186331067 1089 "q-36754" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331067 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535098 true] [17592186331067 1100 "Find a vector equation of the normal line to the surface ${x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=1$ at the point $(0,0,2).$" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331067 1113 #uuid "a7c74ce4-3c4e-5ea4-ab88-89558065f279" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331067 1145 "First, note that we can write the equation of our surface as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}-1=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we set $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}-1$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=0.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point $(0,0,2)$ can be found by computing $∇f(0,0,2).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(0,0,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}-1)i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}-1)j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}-1)k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+\\frac{2y}{9}\\text{ }j+\\frac{z}{2}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(0,0,2) & =2(0)\\text{ }i+\\frac{2(0)}{9}\\text{ }j+\\frac{(2)}{2}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the vector form of the equation of the line that is parallel to $∇f(0,0,2)$ and passes through the point $(0,0,2)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,2⟩+t\\,∇f(0,0,2)=⟨0,\\,0,\\,2⟩+t\\,⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331069 13194139535098 true] [17592186331068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331070 13194139535098 true] [17592186331068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331071 13194139535098 true] [17592186331068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331072 13194139535098 true] [17592186331068 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331073 13194139535098 true] [17592186331068 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535098 true] [17592186331068 1041 "selection" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331068 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331070 13194139535098 true] [17592186331068 1110 #uuid "6f3b0ae0-9f9e-5e3a-9686-db4660f93548" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331069 1034 "⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩+t\\,⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331069 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331069 1111 #uuid "03cd2d07-59f1-5c9d-909e-2170951b37aa" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331070 1034 "⟨0,\\,0,\\,2⟩+t\\,⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331070 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331070 1111 #uuid "d78e9b94-7053-513c-889e-9ac4ee996a7f" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331071 1034 "⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩+t\\,⟨0,\\,0,\\,2⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331071 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331071 1111 #uuid "16b5ac7f-7e44-532e-9c98-2ab0811a023b" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331072 1034 "⟨0,\\,0,\\,2⟩+t\\,⟨0,\\,-1,\\,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331072 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331072 1111 #uuid "b1be908a-3ae9-5e12-9823-793330a24909" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331073 1034 "⟨0,\\,0,\\,-2⟩+t\\,⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331073 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535098 true] [17592186331073 1111 #uuid "c8c38b2c-71a1-501f-83d1-68f8363a1b65" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331074 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331075 13194139535098 true] [17592186331074 1089 "q-71388" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331074 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535098 true] [17592186331074 1100 "Consider the plane curve $2x+y-1=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(1,0).$" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331074 1113 #uuid "e82fe7da-02e3-534e-99f6-4b0ee233facf" 13194139535098 true] [17592186331074 1145 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-1 & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}} \\\\ -1 & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}-2x-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}-2x-y$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=-1.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(1,0)$ can be found by computing $∇f(1,0).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}-2x-y)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}-2x-y)\\,j \\\\  & =(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}-2)\\,i+(-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}-1)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,0) & =(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}-{0}^{2}}}-2)\\,i+(-\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}-{0}^{2}}}-1)\\,j \\\\  & =-i-j \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(1,0)=⟨-1,-1⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(1,0).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-1}{-1} & =\\frac{y-0}{-1} \\\\ 1-x & =-y \\\\ x-y & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535098 true] [175921863